  "contract": {
    "identity": "A checked monotonically increasing u64 counter per section Stream allocates root and child path-version IDs, including a new version on stay. Bus, epoch and group generation are carried by GroupSnapshot.group. Context IDs are separate; a matching context label does not merge paths. These local version IDs must not be substituted directly for the shared stay identity.",
    "ancestry": "Every retained child carries parent_path_id and current phrase_path_index. Each group snapshot carries its previous receipt cut and up to 16 preceding live path IDs with their phrase-parent slots. Candidate sorting and pruning do not renumber IDs.",
    "branch": "Transition records this update: stay, new_context, return, contrast or development. Relation remains the context interpretation and can persist through stay.",
    "raw_score": "Existing base-head survival or exit probability times retrieved context mass, before previous form weight. Original weight multiplication order, ranking and pruning are unchanged. This is not a joint observation potential or a calibrated posterior.",
    "lifetime": "Retired groups lose their owned paths; new roots allocate new IDs. Epoch/new stream resets the counter under a new owner. Counter exhaustion errors rather than wrapping. Failed transition construction is not claimed to be atomic.",
    "allocation": "Fixed parent inventory and scalar metadata only; no new heap allocation sites. Existing form Path/Proposal vectors and snapshot structs are larger."
  },
